  (W, "A script, in Bitcoin, is a short program that decides whether a spend of an output is allowed. Every output carries one, called its output script, and every input that spends it carries another, called its input script. The two are run together by every full node that checks the transaction. This level of the chapter introduces both scripts and the small machine that runs them, because each address kind of the following levels is only a name for a particular output script."),
