  (W, "An input script is the field of a transaction input that provides what the output script being spent demands. Where the output script says what must be shown, the input script shows it. In the earliest scheme the input script consisted entirely of the spender's signature, and for a pay to public key hash output it consists of a signature followed by the public key [BK]. In the language of the specification of pay to script hash, the input script is the scriptSig [B16]."),
